In the heart of Stranglethorn Vale, a Gnome Warlock named Tink adjusted his goggles as his Succubus, Lys, flitted beside him. They had just completed a quest for the Gnomeregan Enclave, and Lys had used her Seduction to keep a group of feral goblins from attacking. Tink marveled at how Lys could vanish into the shadows, allowing him to sneak past patrols. As they rested, Tink thought about why so many Warlocks chose Voidwalkers instead of Succubus. He smiled, knowing that while the Succubus was a powerful companion, the Voidwalker's utility in combat and survival made it the go-to choice for most Warlocks—especially when the questing path was filled with danger and the need for constant protection. 

**Answer:** Voidwalkers provide better threat generation, crowd control, and survival mechanics, making them more versatile for leveling and questing compared to the Succubus. [end of text]


